   "text": "I read the molecule as a Ga-labelled DOTA-type chelator joined to a cyclic peptide through an isoindole. Only the amide-bearing macrocycle carbon, the lysine alpha carbon and the peptide residues carry stereo, as read from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**Chelator.** The 12-membered tetra-aza ring (cyclen) has three N-CH2-COOH arms. The fourth N carries CH2-C(=O)-NH-, which links to a cysteic acid residue, CH(CH2SO3H). Ga is drawn as a label inside the ring with no bonds, so I wrote it as a separate `[Ga]` component.\n\n**Peptide chain.** After cysteic acid, an NH-(CH2)4 chain leads to the alpha carbon of a lysine-type residue. That alpha carbon is bonded to the isoindole nitrogen (a 2H-isoindole carrying a 4-nitro group and a 1-thioether). From its carbonyl the sequence runs:\n\n1. Tyr\n2. Lys(N-isopropyl)\n3. Arg (guanidine)\n4. 2-naphthylalanine\n5. Ala\n6. Cys, whose sulfur bonds to isoindole C1, closing the macrocycle\n7. Lys(N-isopropyl) with a C-terminal NH2\n\n**Stereochemistry.** Working out each centre from the wedges and hashes gives:\n\n| Residue | CIP |\n|---|---|\n| Cysteic acid | R |\n| Isoindole-bearing lysine | S |\n| Tyr | S |\n| Lys(iPr) in the ring | S |\n| Arg | R (D) |\n| 2-Nal | S |\n| Ala | R (D) |\n| Cys | R |\n| C-terminal Lys(iPr) | S |\n\nI converted these to SMILES chirality tags by hand and have not run the string through a parser.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)N[C@@H](CS(=O)(=O)O)C(=O)NCCCC[C@H](n2cc3c([N+](=O)[O-])cccc3c2S4)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(O)cc5)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc6ccccc6c5)C(=O)N[C@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C4)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)C)C(N)=O)CC1.[Ga]"
